docs {
  # Create Award
  
  Creates a new award block for your profile. This endpoint uses the batch update system, so you can create multiple awards in a single request.
  
  ## Request Body
  
  The request uses the batch update format with a `creations` array. Each creation object contains:
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `block_type` | string | ✅ | Must be `"award"` |
  | `section_name` | string | ❌ | Section name (e.g., "awards", "honors", "recognition") |
  | `sort_order` | number | ❌ | Order within section (0 = first) |
  | `data` | object | ✅ | Award data (see below) |
  
  ### Award Data Fields
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `title` | string | ✅ | Award title/name (max 255 chars) |
  | `issuer` | string | ❌ | Organization or person who issued the award (max 255 chars) |
  | `date_received` | string | ❌ | Date award was received in `YYYY-MM-DD` format |
  | `description` | string | ❌ | Description of the award and why it was received |
  | `url` | string | ❌ | URL to more information about the award |
  
  ## Example: Professional Award
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "award",
        "section_name": "awards",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "title": "Innovation Award",
          "issuer": "Tech Industry Association",
          "date_received": "2023-11-20",
          "description": "Recognized for developing an innovative solution that improved system efficiency by 50%.",
          "url": "https://techindustry.org/awards/2023"
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Academic Award
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "award",
        "section_name": "awards",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "title": "Dean's List",
          "issuer": "University of California",
          "date_received": "2022-05-15",
          "description": "Achieved Dean's List recognition for maintaining a GPA of 3.8 or higher for three consecutive semesters."
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Competition Award
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "award",
        "section_name": "awards",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "title": "First Place - Hackathon 2023",
          "issuer": "Tech Conference",
          "date_received": "2023-09-10",
          "description": "Won first place in the annual hackathon competition with a team of 4, building a real-time collaboration tool in 24 hours.",
          "url": "https://techconference.com/hackathon/2023"
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Scholarship Award
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "award",
        "section_name": "awards",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "title": "Merit Scholarship",
          "issuer": "National Science Foundation",
          "date_received": "2021-08-01",
          "description": "Awarded full-tuition scholarship for academic excellence and research contributions in computer science.",
          "url": "https://nsf.gov/scholarships/2021"
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Multiple Awards
  
  You can create multiple awards in a single request:
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "award",
        "section_name": "awards",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "title": "Best Paper Award",
          "issuer": "International Conference on Software Engineering",
          "date_received": "2023-06-15",
          "description": "Recognized for outstanding research paper on distributed systems architecture.",
          "url": "https://icse2023.org/awards"
        }
      },
      {
        "block_type": "award",
        "section_name": "awards",
        "sort_order": 1,
        "data": {
          "title": "Outstanding Contributor",
          "issuer": "Open Source Foundation",
          "date_received": "2022-12-10",
          "description": "Recognized for significant contributions to open source projects, including 1000+ commits and mentoring new contributors."
        }
      },
      {
        "block_type": "award",
        "section_name": "awards",
        "sort_order": 2,
        "data": {
          "title": "Excellence in Leadership",
          "issuer": "Company Leadership Team",
          "date_received": "2023-03-20",
          "description": "Awarded for exceptional leadership in managing cross-functional teams and delivering high-impact projects."
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Minimal Award Entry
  
  Only `title` is required:
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "award",
        "section_name": "awards",
        "data": {
          "title": "Certificate of Achievement"
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Response (200 OK)
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Version updated successfully",
    "data": {
      "version": {
        "id": 12,
        "version_number": 12,
        "created_at": "2024-01-16T15:00:00Z"
      },
      "created_blocks": [108],
      "updated_blocks": [],
      "deleted_blocks": []
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Notes
  
  - Only `title` is required; all other fields are optional
  - Dates must be in `YYYY-MM-DD` format
  - Common award types include: professional recognition, academic honors, competition wins, scholarships, certifications of achievement, etc.
  - `issuer` can be an organization, company, institution, or individual
  - `url` is useful for linking to award announcements, press releases, or verification pages
  - Awards can be sorted chronologically using `sort_order` (most recent first is common)
  - Each request creates a new version, preserving history
}

